The first baseline exposed an important optimization: because each Dickson determinant is homogeneous cubic in the derivative direction, a competent reference algorithm tests projective directions, \(p^2+p+1\), not all \(p^3-1\) nonzero vectors. I’m correcting the Track B claim to the stronger standard algorithm. At \(p=101\) this is still roughly 10,000 exact \(3\times3\) tests (hundreds of thousands of scalar operations), versus the ≤288-operation invariant route.
apply patch
