+The paper's proof displays scalar 4 instead of 16: its Theorem 2.6 system
+sets each parenthesized coefficient to twice the product coefficient, while
+Proposition 2.2 has another outer factor 2.  The missing nonzero factor 4 does
+not affect planarity, but this checker uses the exact coefficient identity.
+
+Track decision.  Track A would be false: Proposition 2.2 is a finite exhaustive
+algorithm and standard finite-field equation solving is efficient in the input
+size when the field is represented explicitly.  This is Track B.  The bundled
+reference follows Proposition 2.2 and quotients scalar multiples, testing
+p^2+p+1 projective derivative matrices for a planar candidate.  The compact
+route instead notices the invariant
